## SQ-ENGM-01 | Done; no mixin or moved-class error; Worldgen and Equipment mod data packs lines
@group B (full pack, fresh world)
@commands prep_srv (swaps all eight builds); boot; `grep -E "Mixing [A-Za-z_.]*(creativecompat|creativemagic|creativeengineering)" logs/latest.log \| wc -l`; `grep -h "mod data packs\|NCH.*not on classpath\|CEConfig" logs/latest.log logs/kubejs/startup.log`
@pass boot reaches Done; no `Mixin apply failed`, `InvalidMixinException`, `ClassNotFoundException` naming a moved class; no `CEConfig not on classpath`; Worldgen and Equipment print `mod data packs on: [...]` naming the five Delight / Upgrade Aquatic packs and `felsic_gear`; `[swaps] config sections ... carried` not needed (values already in the Compat file)
@fails a mixin left in the old json (moved class missing); gate row missing in `CompatMixinPlugin` / `MagicMixinPlugin`
@from batches/r1113/c3_b1.qb
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject Mixin apply failed|InvalidMixinException
bootreject ClassNotFoundException.*com\.SaintAlfonzo
bootreject CEConfig not on classpath|NCH.*not on classpath
bootexpect \[creativeworldgen\] mod data packs on: \[(?=.*farmersdelight)(?=.*fungidelight)(?=.*miners_delight)(?=.*upgrade_aquatic)(?=.*vintagedelight)
bootexpect \[creativeequipment\] mod data packs on: \[.*felsic_gear
shell grep -hE "mod data packs|NCH.*not on classpath|CEConfig" logs/latest.log logs/kubejs/startup.log | cut -c1-250
# r1114: latest.log has no "Mixing" lines (grep -c 0 = exit 1 failed the row); count the mixin configs in debug.log, record only
shell for m in creativecompat creativemagic creativeengineering; do echo "$m $(grep -cE "from (mixins\.)?$m\.mixins\.json" logs/debug.log)"; done
look Worldgen's line also has biomesoplenty now (its pack folder exists since the row was written); the mixin count is for the record

## SQ-ENGM-02 | creativeworldgen packs listed; sky island locatable; driftwood, morels, cave carrots present near spawn
@group B (same boot)
@commands `> datapack list`; `/locate structure creativeengineering:sky_island` and `waystone_ruin` (or `/cdevplace`); `> execute in minecraft:the_nether run locate biome terralith:scarlet_mountains` or the Scarlet biome id; `/zq census` driftwood / deadwood / morel / cave carrot features over a few chunks near spawn
@pass all `creativeworldgen:<mod>` packs listed and enabled; sky island and waystone ruin locatable; wild mushrooms, cave carrots, driftwood present as before (compare SQ-WGE / SQ-CDW census numbers)
@fails a feature file left behind in `kubejs/data/creativeengineering/` (now duplicate) or a pack folder missing `pack.mcmeta`
@from batches/r1113/c3_b1.qb
> datapack list
waitlog data packs? enabled 30
expect creativeworldgen
> locate structure creativeworldgen:sky_island
waitlog (nearest creativeworldgen:sky_island|Could not find) 300
> locate structure creativeworldgen:waystone_ruin_part
waitlog (nearest creativeworldgen:waystone_ruin_part|Could not find|no structure|Unknown|Invalid) 300
> locate biome terralith:scarlet_mountains
waitlog (nearest terralith:scarlet_mountains|Could not find) 300
> forceload add -80 -80 79 79
sleep 60
> zq count -80 50 -80 79 120 79 upgrade_aquatic:driftwood_log
waitlog \[zq\] count upgrade_aquatic:driftwood_log: \d+ 300
> zq count -80 -64 -80 79 120 79 fungidelight:morel_mushroom
waitlog \[zq\] count fungidelight:morel_mushroom: \d+ 300
> zq count -80 -64 -80 79 60 79 miners_delight:wild_cave_carrots
waitlog \[zq\] count miners_delight:wild_cave_carrots: \d+ 300
> forceload remove -80 -80 79 79
look sky island located (ids are creativeworldgen: since the Worldgen carve; the row's creativeengineering: ids are gone); the waystone ruin is a meta structure (its part is the only registered structure: a "Could not find" is not a FAIL, use /cdevplace later); Scarlet Mountains is an Overworld Terralith biome (the row's Nether execute is wrong); the counts near spawn (mostly ocean) are for the record against SQ-WGE / SQ-CDW census numbers: driftwood > 0 expected on this ocean spawn

